## Workflow (agentkit)

Every feature goes spec -> tests -> freeze -> implement. Details, only when a phase is unclear:
`.agentkit/workflow/WORKFLOW.md`. Run tools as `{{python}} .agentkit/bin/agentkit <command>`.

**Session start:** if no hook already printed it, run `status` (10 lines max). Work on one spec phase per session.

### Hard rules
1. Files listed in `{{lock}}` are frozen. Never edit, move, delete or regenerate them, with any tool
   or shell command. If a frozen test looks wrong, stop and tell the human. Only they unfreeze.
2. Never edit `{{lock}}`, `{{unfreeze_log}}`, `agentkit.toml` or `.agentkit/`. Never run
   `git commit --no-verify`, never change `core.hooksPath`, never run `lock unfreeze`.
3. The human owns the gates: spec approval, test approval and `/freeze`. Set a spec to `approved`
   or `tests-approved` only when the human said so in this conversation.
4. Make frozen tests pass honestly: no special-casing test inputs, no skipped or weakened checks.
5. Test names start with requirement IDs (`{{req_id_example}}`), and `trace` must pass.

### Commands
| Need | Command |
|---|---|
| Where are we, what next | `status` |
| Run tests, compact output (never read raw build logs) | `test`, or `test <scope>` |
| Start a spec folder | `new-spec NNN slug` |
| Change phase | `spec-status NNN approved` (also `tests-draft`, `tests-approved`, `done`) |
| Requirement coverage | `trace` or `trace --spec NNN` |
| Save progress before ending a session | `handoff NNN --next "..."` |
| Undo an accidental change to a frozen file | `lock restore` |

### Token discipline
- Read `{{codemap}}` and the spec's API contract before exploring. Open only the files you need.
- While implementing, run targeted tests. Run the full `test` before committing.
- Send verbose work (log digging, wide searches) to a fast-tier subagent if your tool has them.
  Do trivial steps yourself.
- Conventional commits: `spec(NNN): ...`, `test(NNN): ...`, `feat(NNN): ...`, `fix: ...`, `chore: ...`.
